ng the second line."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "G8 lost 15.1 points and took the lead from -11.5 to -26.6, where the engine wanted F8. Black extended a column up the G-file while White's stones on F6 and F7 stood beside it."}, {"turn": 20, "text": "White answered with F8, which lost 18.7 points by the analysis and moved the lead from -26.6 to -7.9. The engine's choice was H6. The 20k had a chance to end the game here and did not take it, so Black was still within reach."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "G9 was the decisive move, the worst of the game at 24.5 points lost. The lead went from -7.9 to -32.4, and the engine's choice was H5. White's reply H5 was that very point, and Black never got closer than 32 points again."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "All JavaScript called the go tools to play moves the player named, or ran inspection/verification code (game-177-inspection.js, game-177-verify.js) that parses boards, counts liberties and area, and replays the actual move history, plus recorder code and notes/log files. Nothing loops over candidate moves or looks ahead; the move choices were hardcoded in each play call.", "stop": false}}